<title>POLAND: Stalexport signs $6 mln contracts.</title>
<headline>Stalexport signs $6 mln contracts.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish steel trader Stalexport SA signed two contracts on selling steel products to Slovakia and the Czech Republic worth a total of $6 million, the company said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Stalexport said the products would be made at the Polish steel mill  Huta Ostrowiec SA but did not give the names of any Slovak or Czech firms involved.</p>
<p>It said the contracts would be carried out by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
